# CTT: rename the Telit LE910Q1 (1bc7:7020) RNDIS network interface to a
# stable name "mdm0", off the eth* pool.
#
# Why: the rndis_host netdev otherwise lands as ethN and races the USB
# wired-LAN dongle for eth0/eth1 — non-deterministic across boots (we have
# observed the Telit taking eth0 and the wired ASIX getting bumped to eth1,
# which breaks the wired-con catch-all and routing). Renaming it to mdm0:
#   - keeps `wired-con` ([match] interface-name=eth*) matching only real
#     Ethernet dongles, so the wired LAN name stays deterministic;
#   - gives ModemManager / NetworkManager / the /modem/ppp check a single
#     fixed interface name to key on regardless of enumeration order.
#
# Telit-VID-scoped (1bc7:7020) — does not affect Quectel or any other device.
#
# VERIFY ON REBOOT: confirm `ip -br link` shows `mdm0` (not ethN) and the
# wired dongle keeps its eth slot. udev net renames can interact with
# systemd .link policies; the image ships empty 73-usb-net-by-mac.link /
# 99-default.link, so this NAME assignment should win — but confirm live.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1bc7", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7020", NAME="mdm0"
